In <1sn4tc$db4@balsam.unca.edu> baswell@cs.unca.edu (Jamie Baswell) writes:

>  As long as I'm here...
>  Anyone else think that shops are WAY too hard to rob, now?  Last time I
>played Nethack (that was when you could run it on an 8088 and 2 disk
>drives), when you stole from a store, sure, the Kops came after you, but
>even if you were surrounded by 12 of them it was no worry.  In fact, it was
>almost good (if you had a decent weapon and some decent armor) because you'd
>end up having a ton of cream pies to eat.  But now they grab up clubs and
>stuff and can really let you have it, if they get you cornered.  I used to
>kill shopkeepers with a good wand or two when they ventured out of the store
>to find me.  ("Excuse me, Bob, didn't you forget to pay?"  <ZAP!>)  But just
>today a shopkeeper jumped two spaces and then hit me about 5 times in one
>turn.  They didn't even notice it when you knocked a hole in their wall,
>until you left the store.  (knocking holes in walls is totally foolish now,
>unless you really think you can kill the shopkeeper, and by the time you can
>do that, chances are you don't need much of anything they have)
>  It's just no fun fighting Kops now when you know the Shopkeeper 'O
>Insta-Death will be coming around the corner at high speed any second to
>slam your face into the wall and kill your level 10 character within 1 turn.
>  An old spoiler-file once mentioned that most of the fun in shops was
>finding the different ways to rob them.  Looks like the newer versions fixed
>all that!  Now you just have to try and keep Fido happy.  <sigh!>

>  (Bah!  Humbug!  Why, back in MY day.....)

I must agree...  I haven't (intentionally & successfully) robbed a shop once
in 3.1.x  I stood in the opposite corner of a shop and tried a wand of digging.
The shop keeper ran across the room, and grabbed the pack off my back before I
fell through (!)  I've never had that happen.  If the shop keepers were slowed
down to realistic human speeds, I think things would be better.

Yet another unrelated subject...  Must monsters always chose to zap DOWN
with a wand of digging?  Everytime I play, I come across two or three zap-happy
kobolds, who manage to get down to level 18 to 20 by repeatedly zapping their
wands of digging.  This is extremely inconveniencing...  trapdoors are frequent
enough in rooms without having them in hallways, altar rooms, shop doorways and
the like.


